[
*1. Current architecture and decision boundary*
#v(0.22em)
This chapter maps the independent Expo/React Native application. Maintain mobile navigation, screen state, API calls, media display, application identity, and release metadata as native product responsibilities rather than browser behavior.
#v(0.35em)
*2. Source map and dependencies*
#v(0.22em)
#text(font: "DejaVu Sans Mono", size: 6.85pt)[apps/mobile/src/NativeApp.tsx · apps/mobile/src/screens · apps/mobile/src/lib/api.ts · app.json · eas.json]
#v(0.28em)
Trace native work from NativeApp.tsx to the screen module and lib/api.ts. Keep Expo configuration, Android version metadata, package identity, and EAS profile decisions in the same release record.
#v(0.35em)
*3. Before you change anything*
#v(0.22em)
Define the desired observable result for native architecture regression checks, identify the affected users and private data, list the routes/screens and database objects touched, and decide whether the change is reversible. Make a before-state record with source commit, current status, error text if any, and a safe test account or record. Never use a live member’s private document, payment proof, or message as a development fixture.
],
[
*4. What to do and how to do it*
#v(0.22em)
1. Locate the screen in the native navigation shell and trace its API calls through lib/api.ts. Check route state, signed media, local preference state, loading/empty/error behavior, and Android package configuration.
#v(0.22em)
2. Implement native UI and API changes together. Keep network calls cancellable or guarded against stale state, and update the language/appearance context rather than duplicating preferences inside individual screens.
#v(0.22em)
3. Run TypeScript compilation and the native architecture test, then test the exact screen on a physical Android device. Validate sign-in, Back, keyboard, media, offline/retry, and state after a short background interruption.
#v(0.22em)
4. Rollback by rebuilding from the last verified source revision. Do not change the Expo project, Android package name, or signing identity merely to bypass a build problem; preserve release continuity.
])
#v(0.45em)
*5. Test, release, and rollback evidence*
#v(0.22em)
Run: #text(font: "DejaVu Sans Mono", size: 7.15pt)[cd apps/mobile && npx tsc --noEmit && node tests/native-architecture.test.mjs]. Then exercise the user journey with the correct actor and a denied actor where authorization applies. Verify the rendered result, database/RPC result, private-media access outcome, notifications if relevant, and server/device logs. Record the approved commit and release identity. If the change fails, stop further writes, return the application to the prior verified revision, preserve evidence, and correct data only through an authorized migration or protected administrative action.
#v(0.42em)
*6. Future growth and maintenance*
#v(0.22em)
At higher mobile usage, cache safe read models locally, preserve drafts carefully, and request only the next page of records instead of refreshing every screen.
#v(0.42em)
