*5. Test, release, and rollback evidence*
#v(0.22em)
Run: #text(font: "DejaVu Sans Mono", size: 7.15pt)[Verify proof prerequisites, payment-review queue visibility, authorized decision, match creation, and participant notifications]. Then exercise the user journey with the correct actor and a denied actor where authorization applies. Verify the rendered result, database/RPC result, private-media access outcome, notifications if relevant, and server/device logs. Record the approved commit and release identity. If the change fails, stop further writes, return the application to the prior verified revision, preserve evidence, and correct data only through an authorized migration or protected administrative action.
#v(0.42em)
